{"id": "EUVD-2026-59532", "enisaUuid": "4ff341be-f4a4-38b7-b118-5ffa5e435e40", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnvmet-tcp: check return value of nvmet_tcp_set_queue_sock\n\nThe return value of nvmet_tcp_set_queue_sock() is currently ignored in\nnvmet_tcp_tls_handshake_done(). If it fails (e.g., due to the socket\nnot being in TCP_ESTABLISHED state), the socket callbacks will not be\nproperly set, leading to queue and socket leakage.\n\nFix this by capturing the return value and calling\nnvmet_tcp_schedule_release_queue() on failure to ensure proper cleanup.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:59:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:45:33", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/41b63ff99e3ef37d08f3693413dae5ede5e79fe1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cba2ee57fd302727aea7d41e9d9cd0969f5df0fb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/22aa70f9a0544643ec37d442b6fcb1833d804462", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7ef789703e2b91775dcb36b2efa46325be31a2a0"], "aliases": ["GHSA-33r9-vmmw-q268", "CVE-2026-74385"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.44, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "028d0d65-b9ba-395f-b401-3e8734af4816", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "675b453e024154dd547921c6e6d5b58747ba7e0e <22aa70f9a0544643ec37d442b6fcb1833d804462"}, {"id": "2d1f2736-a386-38d8-997b-53117cae6d63", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "347f6616-f07f-3b64-ae8a-df5d1db0aa13", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "675b453e024154dd547921c6e6d5b58747ba7e0e <7ef789703e2b91775dcb36b2efa46325be31a2a0"}, {"id": "37c45747-7db1-3b1c-b5af-21ff2009d5cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "675b453e024154dd547921c6e6d5b58747ba7e0e <41b63ff99e3ef37d08f3693413dae5